# Shell heartbeat (terminal progress)

When the user may watch the terminal, long **`Shell`** commands must emit a visible heartbeat so the session does not look hung.

## When required

Use heartbeat for **Medium** or **Slow** tier commands per **`shell-hygiene.mdc`** (expected **>15s**), including:

- `.\scripts\ci\agent-compile-check.ps1`
- `dotnet build`, `dotnet test`, `npm run …`, Docker, Terraform apply
- Any command whose **child stdout/stderr is redirected** (silent terminal until exit)

## When to skip

Skip for **Fast** tier: chained `git status` / `git diff` / `git log`, `gh pr view`, `Get-ChildItem`, and anything expected to finish in **<15s**.

## Message format

Every **8 seconds** while the child runs:

```text
STILL EXECUTING... HH:mm:ss
```

Use `Get-Date -Format 'HH:mm:ss'` (24-hour). Emit with **`Write-Host`** so lines appear on the host, not inside a redirect file.

## How to run (one Shell invocation)

Wrap the real work inside the **same** `Shell` call as the heartbeat loop. Do **not** start a second shell for progress lines.

```powershell
$intervalSec = 8
$repoRoot = (Get-Location).Path

$job = Start-Job -ScriptBlock {
    param($Root)
    Set-StrictMode -Version Latest
    Set-Location -LiteralPath $Root
    & .\scripts\ci\agent-compile-check.ps1 -ProjectPath 'ArchLucid.Core/ArchLucid.Core.csproj'
    exit $LASTEXITCODE
} -ArgumentList $repoRoot

try {
    while ($job.State -eq 'Running') {
        Write-Host ("STILL EXECUTING... {0}" -f (Get-Date -Format 'HH:mm:ss'))
        Start-Sleep -Seconds $intervalSec
    }

    $output = Receive-Job $job -Wait -AutoRemoveJob
    if ($null -ne $output) { $output | ForEach-Object { Write-Host $_ } }

    if ($job.JobStateInfo.State -eq 'Failed') {
        $reason = $job.ChildJobs[0].JobStateInfo.Reason
        if ($null -ne $reason) { Write-Error $reason }
        exit 1
    }

    exit 0
}
finally {
    if ($job.State -eq 'Running') {
        Stop-Job $job -Force
        Remove-Job $job -Force
    }
}
```

Adapt the script block for the actual command. Always **`exit $LASTEXITCODE`** inside the job when the child is an external executable.

## Repo scripts

When a **`.ps1`** already redirects child stdout/stderr, add the heartbeat loop there (e.g. inside `Invoke-TimedExternalProcess` in **`agent-compile-check.ps1`**) so agents call the script directly without copying the wrapper.
